SQLite 3.53.4

SQLite's authors have dedicated its code and documentation to the public domain.
The adjacent LICENSE reproduces the public-domain notice and blessing from
sqlite3.h, with the C comment markers removed. The SPDX license identifier for
that text is blessing.

Upstream copyright statement: https://www.sqlite.org/copyright.html
Official source archive:
https://www.sqlite.org/2026/sqlite-amalgamation-3530400.zip

fsim builds the unmodified sqlite3.c amalgamation as an internal static library
with serialized thread support and dynamic extension loading disabled. The
SQLite command-line shell is included in the upstream archive but is not built
or installed by fsim.
